From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: a shared image section not aligned to the host page is mapped private

Two GameMaker games failed at image load on a tester's standard PS5
(2026-10-31, klog/tester-ut-dr-2026-10-31, not in the tree): "unaligned shared
mapping ... not supported", "Could not map ... shared section .mydata", and for
the 64-bit one "failed to start ...: c000007b". The GameMaker runner has a
4 KiB section marked shared and writable (.mydata) at a 4 KiB offset. Such a
section is mapped MAP_SHARED from the image's shared-sections file, which needs
whole host pages; the PS5's host page is 16 KiB, so map_file_into_view skipped
the mmap and refused the writable fallback. On Linux, with 4 KiB pages, it
never happens.

Under __PROSPERO__, a shared writable section whose start or size is not a
multiple of the host page is now mapped as an ordinary section: read in from
the image and written in place, with one WARN per section. Only the sharing of
that section between two running copies of the same program is lost (Windows
programs use it for single-instance flags; games do not rely on it). The offset
into the shared-sections file still advances past it, so a later aligned shared
section maps its own bytes. An aligned shared section is mapped as before.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4285,6 +4285,7 @@
     IMAGE_DATA_DIRECTORY *imports, *dir;
     NTSTATUS status = STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES;
     int i;
+    BOOL shared;
     off_t pos;
     struct stat st;
     char *header_end;
@@ -4375,8 +4376,21 @@
             goto done;
         }
 
-        if ((sec[i].Characteristics & IMAGE_SCN_MEM_SHARED) &&
-            (sec[i].Characteristics & IMAGE_SCN_MEM_WRITE))
+        shared = (sec[i].Characteristics & IMAGE_SCN_MEM_SHARED) && (sec[i].Characteristics & IMAGE_SCN_MEM_WRITE);
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        /* A shared writable section needs a MAP_SHARED mapping of whole host pages, 16 KiB here: GameMaker's runner
+         * has a 4 KiB .mydata at a 4 KiB offset, which failed the image (c000007b). Such a section is mapped
+         * private instead, read in and written in place; only its sharing between two running copies of the same
+         * program is lost. */
+        if (shared && ((sec[i].VirtualAddress | map_size) & host_page_mask))
+        {
+            WARN_(module)( "%s shared section %.8s at %x size %lx is not host-page aligned: mapped private\n",
+                           debugstr_us(nt_name), sec[i].Name, sec[i].VirtualAddress, map_size );
+            pos += map_size;   /* the next shared section's bytes follow this one's in shared_fd */
+            shared = FALSE;
+        }
+#endif
+        if (shared)
         {
             TRACE_(module)( "%s mapping shared section %.8s at %p off %x (%x) size %lx (%lx) flags %x\n",
                             debugstr_us(nt_name), sec[i].Name, ptr + sec[i].VirtualAddress,
-- 
